    "title": "Dana White blunty breaks silence on huge UFC White House main event rumour ahead of Ilia Topuria vs Justin Gaethje",
    "text": "DANA WHITE has addressed claims that a historic fight set to land on the UFC’s White House card fell through due to money issues. Lightweight champion Ilia Topuria will top the bill of the UFC’s ‘Freedom 250’ card on June 14 in a unification bout with interim titleholder Justin Gaethje. Sign up to The Irish Sun’s daily newsletter Thank you! Ilia Topuria tops the bill of the UFC’s White House card on June 14 against Justin GaethjeCredit: SHUTTERSTOCK A fight with pound-for-pound king Islam Makhachev was briefly on the cards for ‘El Matador’Credit: GETTY But an even bigger fight was in the works for Topuria just days before the announcement of his showdown with Gaethje. The promotion were working on a champion vs champion bout between Topuria and his welterweight counterpart Islam Makhachev. The fight, which has been on MMA fans’ wishlists for well over a year, didn’t come to fruition. A public war of words between both men has ensued, with Makhachev blaming Topuria’s financial demands for the fight fall through. He wrote on X: “I got the call and accepted the fight at the White House. “The next day, I was told [Topuria] asked for an unrealistic purse. “The UFC declined, and he pulled out.” Makhachev’s claim that the pair aren’t topping the White House card due to Topuria pricing himself out was this week put to White. Most read in Sport SUN VEGAS WELCOME OFFER: GET UP TO £100 BONUS And the UFC’s long-time President and CEO gave an incredibly blunt answer to the question. During a live stream with Adin Ross, he said: “That’s not true. That’s not true.” UFC White House Card In Full Ilia Topuria v Justin Gaethje – Lightweight title unification fight Alex Pereira vs Cyril Gane – Interim heavyweight title fight Sean O’Malley vs Aiemann Zahabi – men’s bantamweight bout Mauricio Ruffy vs Michael Chandler – lightweight bout Bo Nickal vs Kyle Daukaus – middleweight bout Diego Lopes vs Steve Garcia – featherweight bout White added: “The most important thing for me is to have fights that make sense. “Fights that make sense with the division rankings, but also fighters I can count on and know will show up on fight night.” Topuria, who hasn’t fought since his brutal first-round KO of Charles Oliveira last June, has also denied suggestions that a fight with Makhachev crumbled due to financial demands. UFC boss Dana White insists Ilia Topuria didn’t price himself out of a fight with Islam MakhachevCredit: getty He told Marca: “I received the call from the UFC and they said I could still be on the White House card fighting Islam Makhachev. “Dana White came out saying he’d announce the entire card in two days. “So I thought if I was there, it would be against Islam. “Suddenly, I was called and told that Islam was injured and that I would go against Justin Gaethje. “There were points of the negotiation that we were debating, but it is secondary.” Comments",
